  "reason": "Evidence: config_004 (scvi_n200, singleprofile) achieved 0.520 acc vs config_001 (pca_n2000, singleprofile) at 0.485, showing learned RNA representations beat linear ones. config_010 (resnet50 image-only) at 0.208 confirms image is currently weak. Uncertainty: We have not yet tested scgpt, a third learned RNA encoder, and the encoder choice is foundational for all subsequent multiprofile and multimodal experiments. Question: Does scgpt outperform scvi_n200 in the same singleprofile, rna_only setting? This is a clean single-variable comparison (only the RNA encoder changes from config_004). Why this is best: Completing the encoder ranking (pca < scvi vs scgpt) before introducing additional variables (multiprofile, aggregation, fusion) ensures that all future experiments build on the best-known RNA representation. If scgpt is substantially better, it reshapes the entire search strategy; if comparable, it confirms scvi_n200 as the default and we can next isolate the multiprofile/aggregation question with confidence."
